From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chijure <chijure@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] twrpTar: avoid GUI calls in forked children

createTarFork() and extractTarFork() run the tar work in a child created
by fork(). The child inherits the GUI console and DataManager mutexes in
whatever state other recovery threads held them, so gui_msg(), gui_err()
and LOGERR() can block forever in the child while the parent waits on the
progress pipe.

On the LG D625 this hung every /system backup when the split-archive
notifications ran. Error paths in the same children had the same hazard
and would hang the UI instead of reporting the failure.

Children now write messages straight to the unbuffered recovery log. The
parent still reports the failure through Wait_For_Child() and the normal
backup/restore error handling.
---
--- a/twrpTar.cpp
+++ b/twrpTar.cpp
@@ -53,6 +53,13 @@
 #include "set_metadata.h"
 #endif //ndef BUILD_TWRPTAR_MAIN
 
+// The createTarFork() and extractTarFork() children, and everything they call,
+// inherit the GUI and DataManager mutexes in whatever state other recovery
+// threads held them during fork(). Calling gui_*() or LOGERR() there can
+// deadlock, so children only write to the log; the parent reports the failure
+// after Wait_For_Child().
+#define TAR_CHILD_ERR(...) fprintf(stdout, "E:" __VA_ARGS__)
+
